{"annotationScore": 5.0, "comments": [{"commentType": "FUNCTION", "texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "id": "P01592", "source": "UniProtKB"}], "value": "Serves to link two monomer units of either IgM or IgA. In the case of IgM, the J chain-joined dimer is a nucleating unit for the IgM pentamer, and in the case of IgA it induces dimers and/or larger polymers. It also helps to bind these immunoglobulins to secretory component"}]}, {"commentType": "SUBUNIT", "texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "id": "32029686", "source": "PubMed"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "id": "32029689", "source": "PubMed"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "id": "37095205", "source": "PubMed"}], "value": "Part of the secretory IgA (sIgA) complex that consists of two, four or five IgA monomers, and two additional non-Ig polypeptides, namely the JCHAIN and the secretory component (the proteolytic product of PIGR) (PubMed:32029686). Part of the secretory IgM (sIgM) complex that consists of five IgM monomers, and two additional non-Ig polypeptides, namely the JCHAIN and the secretory component (the proteolytic product of PIGR) (PubMed:32029686, PubMed:32029689). JCHAIN-containing IgM interacts (via CH4 domain) with FCRM (via Ig-like domain) (PubMed:37095205)"}]}, {"commentType": "SUBCELLULAR LOCATION", "subcellularLocations": [{"location": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "id": "P01592", "source": "UniProtKB"}], "id": "SL-0243", "value": "Secreted"}}]}], "entryAudit": {"entryVersion": 200, "firstPublicDate": "1986-07-21", "lastAnnotationUpdateDate": "2026-11-04", "lastSequenceUpdateDate": "2009-10-13", "sequenceVersion": 4}, "entryType": "UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)", "extraAttributes": {"countByCommentType": {"FUNCTION": 1, "SUBCELLULAR LOCATION": 1, "SUBUNIT": 1}, "countByFeatureType": {"Beta strand": 13, "Chain": 1, "Disulfide bond": 5, "Glycosylation": 1, "Helix": 1, "Modified residue": 1, "Signal": 1, "Turn": 2}, "uniParcId": "UPI00